      },
      "message": "fix(generators): exclude mock instructions and CSRs by default\n\nMock/test data (instructions, CSRs, etc. from the Xmock extension) was\nappearing in generated artifacts like encoding.h, which is undesirable\nfor standard downstream consumers like Spike, ACTs, and the Sail model.\n\nThis change:\n- Adds is_mock_item() helper function to detect mock items by:\n  - Name containing 'mock' (case-insensitive)\n  - Being defined by an extension containing 'mock' in its name\n- Adds exclude_mock parameter to load_instructions() and load_csrs()\n  (default: True) to filter out mock items\n- Adds --include-mock flag to all generators (c_header, Go, sverilog)\n  for cases where mock items are intentionally needed\n- Adds logging to report how many mock items were filtered\n\nMock items are now excluded by default but can be included when needed\nfor testing by passing --include-mock to the generator scripts.\n\nCloses #1148",
